# UserDashboard (C#)

C# / WinForms port of `UserDashboard.ps1`. A desktop dashboard for managing
Active Directory users on a domain-joined Windows machine.

## Features (parity with the PowerShell version)

- DataGridView listing every AD user (excluding service / built-in accounts)
- Multi-token AND search with quoted-phrase support (e.g. `smith admin`, `"global shop"`)
- Group filter dropdown
- **Inline cell editing** of First Name / Middle Initials / Last Name / Display Name
  → writes straight back to AD on commit
- Right-click row context menu:
  - Reset Password (with password generator + live requirements checklist)
  - Disable / Enable User (label flips to match current state)
  - Manage Security Groups (checkbox list of available security groups)
- "Add User" dialog modeled on the AD `New Object - User` wizard
  (auto-suggests SAM from First/Initial/Last, UPN suffix dropdown, pre-Win2000 logon)
- CSV Import (bulk create users) and CSV Export (current grid view)
- Per-day audit log at `C:\GSS\UserDashboard\Log\audit_yyyy-MM-dd.csv`
- Disabled accounts are tinted light-red and italicized in the grid

## Project layout

```
UserDashboard/
├── UserDashboard.csproj        .NET 8 / WinForms project file
├── app.manifest                DPI-aware, asInvoker
├── Program.cs                  Entry point + AD preflight
├── Constants.cs                Brand colors, excluded users/groups, audit dir
├── MainForm.cs                 Main dashboard window
├── Models/
│   └── AdUserInfo.cs           Cached snapshot of one AD user
├── Services/
│   ├── AdService.cs            All AD operations
│   ├── AuditLogger.cs          CSV audit log
│   └── PasswordHelper.cs       Validation rules + secure random generator
└── Forms/
    ├── AddUserForm.cs          "New Object - User" dialog
    ├── ResetPasswordForm.cs    Password reset dialog
    ├── ManageGroupsForm.cs     Group membership dialog
    └── PasswordChecklist.cs    Reusable live requirements checklist control
```

## Build & run

Requires .NET 8 SDK on Windows.

```powershell
dotnet restore
dotnet build -c Release
dotnet run -c Release
```

Or publish a single-file exe:

```powershell
dotnet publish -c Release -r win-x64 --self-contained false /p:PublishSingleFile=true
```

The resulting `UserDashboard.exe` will be in `bin/Release/net8.0-windows/win-x64/publish/`.

## Runtime requirements

- Windows 10 / 11 or Windows Server (2016+).
- Machine joined to an Active Directory domain.
- The launching user needs read access to the domain (and write access to whatever
  attributes / groups they intend to modify).
- No RSAT / `ActiveDirectory` PowerShell module is required — the C# port talks
  to AD directly via `System.DirectoryServices` and
  `System.DirectoryServices.AccountManagement`.

## Notable porting decisions vs. the PowerShell version

| PowerShell | C# port |
|---|---|
| `Get-ADUser` / `Set-ADUser` | `DirectoryEntry` + `DirectorySearcher` (and `UserPrincipal` for password / enable ops) |
| `Get-ADGroup` / `Add-ADGroupMember` | `GroupPrincipal` from `AccountManagement` |
| `Get-ADDomain` | `Domain.GetCurrentDomain()` + RootDSE query |
| `LastLogonDate` (a synthesized PS property) | `lastLogonTimestamp` LDAP attribute (replicated; ~14-day resolution) |
| `Set-ADAccountPassword -Reset` | `UserPrincipal.SetPassword` |
| `Disable-ADAccount` / `Enable-ADAccount` | `UserPrincipal.Enabled = false/true; Save()` |
| `Import-Csv` | Hand-rolled RFC-4180 reader in `MainForm.ReadCsv` (no NuGet dependency) |
| `Export-Csv -Append` audit log | `AuditLogger.Write` (file-locked, UTF-8) |
| `New-RandomPassword` (uses `Get-Random`) | `PasswordHelper.Generate` (uses `RandomNumberGenerator`, cryptographically secure) |
| `Add-Type -AssemblyName ...` for WinForms | `<UseWindowsForms>true</UseWindowsForms>` in csproj |

### Things you may want to revisit

1. **Threading.** AD enumeration runs on the UI thread, just like the PS script.
   On large domains you'll want to wrap `LoadUsers` / `LoadAllUsers` in a `Task.Run`
   and `Invoke` results back to the UI.
2. **`lastLogonTimestamp` resolution.** The replicated attribute is only
   updated every ~14 days. For per-second accuracy, query each DC's
   non-replicated `lastLogon` and take the maximum.
3. **Hard-coded audit path.** `C:\GSS\UserDashboard\Log` matches the PowerShell
   version. Move it into `appsettings.json` if you want it configurable.
4. **CSV import dependency.** The hand-rolled reader handles the CSV format
   the PowerShell version's `Import-Csv` accepts. If you want fancier handling
   (different delimiters, type conversion, etc.) drop in `CsvHelper`.
